{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UpfqWhWk37E4foEDRJoTZX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey context:\n1. **Core method**: Simple static embedding-distance mining as a reliable zero-cost baseline for contrastive code retrieval\n2. **D062 checkpoint selection criterion effect (+16.3pp)**: This seems to be a methodological finding about how checkpoint selection criterion affects results\n3. **Current dual framing**: A (criterion dominates) vs B (mining + methodology)\n4. **UniXcoder null result**: 0.37pp span across strategies — no meaningful differentiation on encoder-only architecture\n\n\n5. **Statistical limitations**: Only 3 seeds provide limited power to detect differences, and the SWE-bench out-of-distribution failure is stark — neural retrieval collapses to 0.04 R@1 while BM25 maintains 0.2733\n\nNow I'm looking at the actual Qwen results across different seeds and strategies to see what variation exists in the data. Looking at the embedding versus random performance across seeds, I'm noticing something odd—Qwen's s44 actually performs worse with embedding distance than with random initialization, which breaks the pattern I see in s43. StarCoder shows a similar issue where the embedding approach underperforms random on s42, suggesting these improvements aren't consistent across different random seeds.\n\nAcross all three encoders, the effect sizes are either shrinking or disappearing entirely at full scale compared to the pilot results, and I'm particularly concerned that UniXcoder shows no differentiation at all. The fundamental problem is that with only three seeds and such inconsistent results, I don't have enough statistical power to confidently claim embedding helps, especially when downstream validation on SWE-bench isn't possible.\n\nNow I'm realizing the D062 checkpoint selection criterion effect might be inflating the results — the +16.3pp difference could be an artifact of choosing checkpoints by R@1 versus validation loss rather than a genuine finding about embedding quality.\n\nI need to wait for the remaining runs to complete across Qwen and StarCoder before I can properly assess which tier this work falls into, since the final results depend on whether this effect holds up across different model families.\n\nIn the best case, embedding mining consistently outperforms random baselines, the checkpoint selection criterion becomes a publishable methodological contribution, and the null result on UniXcoder cleanly establishes an architecture boundary. In the median case, the improvements are smaller and more inconsistent across seeds, which would weaken the narrative around both the mining approach and the checkpoint selection insight.\n\nIn the worst case, the mining advantage disappears entirely at scale, the BM25 negatives don't help, and the whole story collapses—leaving me with either a negative result paper or a methodology-focused piece instead.\n\nNow I'm examining the actual metrics more carefully, particularly the Qwen embedding results across seeds to see whether the pilot data holds up at full scale. I'll use the m2_full_qwen_continued results as the authoritative source since they're more recent. Looking at the performance deltas across both models, embedding distance shows mixed results—it helps Qwen by about 1pp on seed 43 but hurts on seed 44, while dataflow awareness barely moves the needle. StarCoder's embedding approach actually underperforms the baseline, which is surprising.\n\nNow I'm thinking through what metrics really matter to validate the core claims: the embedding versus random delta across seeds, how consistent those results are, whether both encoders show the same pattern, what BM25 tells us about the CoCoHaNeRe narrative, and whether the checkpoint criterion's large effect size holds up as a robust methodological finding.\n\nFor the best-case scenario, the remaining seeds would confirm that embeddings outperform random baselines—around 1 percentage point for Qwen and 0.5 for StarCoder—with tight cross-seed consistency under 1 percentage point. BM25 negatives would clearly hurt performance, validating the correction approach, and the checkpoint criterion's 16.3 percentage point boost would emerge as a genuine methodological contribution rather than an artifact. RepoBench-R would show consistent rankings, the UniXcoder null would make sense as a scale boundary issue, and the paper would position itself as a systematic mining study with a solid methodological finding and clear boundary conditions.\n\nIn a median outcome, embeddings show mixed signals across seeds—some positive, some neutral or slightly negative—with a mean effect around 0.3-0.8 percentage points where confidence intervals might cross zero. BM25 performs roughly like random, which doesn't kill the narrative but requires repositioning. The checkpoint criterion effect would still exist but might feel incremental to reviewers. RepoBench-R results would be modest or unclear, and the UniXcoder failure would weaken any generalization claims, forcing the paper to lean heavily on the checkpoint criterion as the main methodological contribution while framing mining as a sometimes-helpful technique tied to representation geometry.\n\nThe worst case would be if embedding mining performs at or below random across all seeds and encoders, with 95% confidence intervals firmly including zero, and BM25 doesn't show clear harm either. I'm checking what results I actually have for the Qwen embedding experiments across different seeds and configurations. The pilot run showed a +2.0pp improvement, but I need to verify which seeds have complete data for the full experiment—it looks like embedding_s42 and some dataflow runs are still missing.\n\nFor prioritizing what to work on next, the most critical gaps are the StarCoder embedding results across seeds to see if they replicate the pattern, followed by the dataflow and BM25 experiments. Now I'm trying to make sense of that D062 checkpoint selection criterion effect mentioned in the user's data—I need to trace through what that +16.3pp improvement actually represents in the results. The checkpoint selection criterion seems to create a substantial methodological effect—around 16.3 percentage points—that could actually overshadow the mining strategy differences themselves. I'm weighing two ways to frame this: either emphasizing that the criterion choice dominates the results, or presenting both the mining findings and the criterion effect as separate contributions. Now I need to work through the actual performance numbers for the remaining experiments, starting with what the Qwen embedding results look like across different seeds. I need to reframe this around the three scenarios as planning frameworks rather than predictions, then organize everything against those five core contributions and the pending experimental results that will determine which scenario plays out.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23527,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23527},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c0e5fc7-21e9-4d2a-a44d-ab2cc9700b59","uuid":"7901a5d0-c9e4-4e12-af22-3cdf42248643"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UpfqWhWk37E4foEDRJoTZX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Embedding mining shows consistent positive effect across both decoder-only encoders; BM25 confirms CoCoHaNeRe correction; checkpoint criterion effect provides strong second contribution\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"StarCoder remaining seeds (embed_s43, s44) recover to positive Δ, mean ≥+0.3pp (s42 was outlier due to early-stop artifact)\"\n      - \"Qwen 3-seed mean embed-random Δ ≥ +0.8pp with all seeds non-negative\"\n      - \"BM25 negatives clearly harm (Δ ≤ -1pp vs random), confirming CoCoHaNeRe artifact hypothesis\"\n      - \"D062 checkpoint criterion effect (+16.3pp) replicates across encoders and seed pairs\"\n      - \"RepoBench-R (plan_004) shows consistent strategy ranking with 95% CIs non-overlapping for embed vs random\"\n      - \"UniXcoder null is cleanly attributable to model scale (125M saturates regardless of strategy)\"\n    number_ranges:\n      qwen_embed_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [0.8, 1.5]\n      starcoder_embed_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [0.3, 1.0]\n      bm25_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [-3.0, -1.0]\n      checkpoint_criterion_effect_pp: [12.0, 20.0]\n      repobench_embed_vs_random_R1_pp: [0.5, 2.0]\n      cross_seed_std_within_strategy_pp: [0.3, 1.5]\n      bootstrap_95ci_excludes_zero: true\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Framing B 完全成立。Paper = systematic mining study + methodological contribution。\n      Claim 1: 简单 embedding mining 在两个 decoder-only encoder 上一致提供 reliable zero-cost improvement。\n      Claim 2 (exploratory): dataflow 与 representation geometry 交互，UniXcoder null 作为 scale boundary condition 增强故事（\"effect requires sufficient model capacity\"）。\n      额外贡献：checkpoint selection criterion 作为独立 methodological finding (+16.3pp > mining effect)，\n      为社区提供 evaluation protocol 建议。BM25 harm 验证 CoCoHaNeRe 修正叙事。\n      SWE-bench OOD failure 简要提及为 limitation（in-distribution retrieval ≠ cross-repo generalization），\n      RepoBench-R 替代作为 held-out evaluation。3 seeds + bootstrap CI 足够支撑 claims。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Embedding mining effect exists but small and seed-dependent; BM25 neutral; criterion effect is main robust finding; need narrative pivot to methodology-first framing\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Qwen 3-seed mean embed-random Δ = +0.3–0.8pp，但 95% CI 下界接近零或轻微包含零\"\n      - \"StarCoder embed mean Δ 在 -0.2 to +0.3pp，不显著（s42 negative confirmed by pattern）\"\n      - \"BM25 ≈ random（Δ within ±0.5pp）— CoCoHaNeRe narrative pivot needed\"\n      - \"D062 checkpoint criterion effect robust（+10–16pp），成为 paper 最强贡献\"\n      - \"RepoBench-R shows directional consistency but CIs overlap\"\n      - \"UniXcoder null + StarCoder weak = 'effect is encoder-specific, not universal'\"\n      - \"3 seeds 对 <1pp effect 统计力度不足，reviewer 会质疑\"\n    number_ranges:\n      qwen_embed_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [0.3, 0.8]\n      starcoder_embed_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [-0.2, 0.3]\n      bm25_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [-0.5, 0.5]\n      checkpoint_criterion_effect_pp: [10.0, 16.0]\n      repobench_embed_vs_random_R1_pp: [0.0, 0.8]\n      cross_seed_std_within_strategy_pp: [1.5, 3.0]\n      bootstrap_95ci_excludes_zero: false\n    narrative_direction: >\n      切换到 Framing A：checkpoint selection criterion dominates mining strategy。\n      主贡献重排：(1) 发现 checkpoint 选择标准对 reported performance 的影响（+10-16pp）远大于 mining strategy 差异（<1pp），\n      揭示领域内 evaluation methodology 系统性问题；(2) 在此框架下，embedding mining 作为 controlled experiment 的一个 condition，\n      在 Qwen 上有 marginal positive signal，但非 universal；(3) representation geometry 分析解释 why effect is encoder-dependent。\n      Claims 调整：将 \"reliable improvement\" 弱化为 \"conditional improvement on saturated-geometry encoders\"。\n      UniXcoder null + StarCoder weak 不再是 limitation 而是 evidence for geometry hypothesis。\n      BM25 neutral → 不能 claim CoCoHaNeRe 的 BM25 proxy 有害，改为 \"mining strategy choice matters less than evaluation methodology\"。\n      SWE-bench 完全不提。RepoBench-R 作为 supplementary validation。\n      温度消融（plan_021）变为 must-have 来排除 regime-specificity。\n      Statistical framing：承认 3 seeds underpowered for <1pp effects，用 effect size + CI 报告而非 p-value。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Mining strategy effect indistinguishable from noise at full scale; only checkpoint criterion effect survives as contribution; complete reframe required\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Qwen embed-random mean Δ < +0.3pp，95% CI 宽且包含零（seed variance > effect）\"\n      - \"StarCoder embed consistently ≤ random（mean Δ ≤ 0pp），反驳 pilot pattern\"\n      - \"BM25 ≈ random 或 BM25 slightly positive → CoCoHaNeRe narrative 完全失效\"\n      - \"RepoBench-R 无法区分策略（pool size 效应吞没 strategy effect）\"\n      - \"Plan_019 pool sensitivity 显示 pool>100 时 strategy ranking 反转或消失\"\n      - \"UniXcoder + StarCoder + Qwen large variance = 'no evidence mining strategy matters at this scale'\"\n      - \"D062 checkpoint criterion effect 仍然 robust（唯一幸存发现）\"\n      - \"SWE-bench OOD failure + 无外部验证 = reviewer concern 无法化解\"\n    number_ranges:\n      qwen_embed_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [-0.3, 0.3]\n      starcoder_embed_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [-1.0, 0.0]\n      bm25_vs_random_mean_R1_pp: [-0.3, 0.5]\n      checkpoint_criterion_effect_pp: [10.0, 18.0]\n      repobench_embed_vs_random_R1_pp: [-0.5, 0.5]\n      cross_seed_std_within_strategy_pp: [2.0, 5.0]\n      bootstrap_95ci_excludes_zero: false\n    narrative_direction: >\n      完全 reframe。两个候选方向（仍冲 EMNLP Main）：\n      方向 1 — \"Checkpoint Selection Criterion Matters More Than Mining Strategy for Code Retrieval\"：\n      核心贡献变为 methodological finding — 在 controlled 3-strategy × 3-seed × 3-encoder 实验中，\n      checkpoint 选择标准（R@1 vs val_loss）造成 +10-18pp 报告差异，而 mining strategy 贡献 <0.3pp。\n      这是对 contrastive code retrieval 社区的 evaluation methodology warning。\n      Supporting evidence: representation geometry 分析解释 why strategies fail to differentiate（\n      decoder-only encoders 的 pretrained geometry 已经足够好，hard mining 无法 further improve）。\n      方向 2 — \"Why Hard Negative Mining Doesn't Scale for Code Retrieval: A Negative Result Study\"：\n      Pilot → full scale degradation pattern 本身作为贡献。分析 scale-dependent factors：\n      (a) full-scale random baseline 更强（更多 naturally hard negatives）；\n      (b) pretrained decoder-only encoders 的 representation quality 使 mining signal marginal；\n      (c) seed variance at this effect size 使 reported gains unreliable。\n      两个方向都保留 CodeQL pipeline 作为 practical contribution + geometry analysis 作为 explanatory tool。\n      UniXcoder null 成为 corroborating evidence。SWE-bench 不提。\n      必须额外做：(a) 更多 seeds（5-10）确认 null；(b) scaling analysis（data size vs effect）；(c) 与 1-2 个 published mining paper 做 reproduction attempt 验证其 claims 在我们 setting 下也不 hold。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23527,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23527},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c0e5fc7-21e9-4d2a-a44d-ab2cc9700b59","uuid":"b7f68672-aff4-4a75-84e4-b380ed38acb1"}
